e of  oblivion and the knotted gland from his  body  the bearer of the glimpse is filled with  a sense of emptiness their surroundings  turn into a muted joyless world their  mind slows and their limbs grow heavy  while the not a gland is a gland that  beats irregularly almost as if there  were two hearts in it this is the final  gland we need we rip  out the gland out of the head's tongue  almost as if the head was the  spirit or soul of the toy sport taking  it back to the old prisoner he calls us  naive going through all this hardship  for one person when only he will ascend  not us and says that we should be  honored to be able to see the ascension  of another being  the old prisoner says that we are just  an empty shell with only instinct and  flesh  left without purpose led by false idols  and that if even for an instant he will  let us bask in the truth and to witness  his ascension  furthermore he rambles on how this is  what it must feel like to be picked  among the many to rule over the lesser  souls  how fate favors those who act and not  those who sit there with no purpose  and that the maggots of this place bow  and scrape before their gods while their  lives unravel thread by thread  in a pile of utter meaninglessness with  the sacred glands in hand he leaves and  goes down the hole  when we follow him we get to see his  true form but there's a problem  everything was wrong he had visions of  ascending into a new life  but now it's all just darkness and  shallow water these visions weren't of  him  but of us and our ascension he's  questioning why we should be allowed to  leave but the rest remain stuck  in falgrim calling this unjust now his  goals have changed  now that he can't descend he won't let  anyone else ascend  sester ganesa brings up to us that when  we take the twice boring land how  us taking these glands was almost like  we were destined to almost as if it was  fate  and then also tells us to not  overindulge she mentions how a heretic  