ester ganesa is just a  vessel now where as we stated when  discussing the order  our spirit will live on past the age of  our body as now we are just immortal  the body is just a vessel for us to pour  ourselves into  and use until we see fit kind of like  how we've been using the shells  throughout our journey  bodies we inhabit until we discard them  in replace of another or to show our  true form  that's the ending of mortal shell before  we head out though i know this is a lot  of information so i wanted to summarize  what we've gone through  it won't be as detailed but if you want  to get the absolute bare minimum  understanding of what's going on with  the game then  here it is we as the foundling someone  with no purpose at the moment of our  arrival  meet a prisoner who gives us that  purpose he asks us for a favor which is  to help us retrieve these sacred glands  so that they can heal him you as the  foundling go to three  areas the shrine of ash the crypt of  martyr and the seed of infinity  battling your way through to meet the  end bosses who possess the sacred glands  these are the founders of each of the  group's religious beliefs in all the  areas everyone has some sort of  religious belief  but they're all different and each god  they believe in is also different with  the end goal of having some sort of  spiritual connection with their god  in whatever way they believe the shrine  of ash whose god is imrad believes in  self-sacrifice by fire to feel a  stronger bond between them and the god  the crypt of martyr worshipers enshrine  themselves in ice so that they can be  reborn when the god  the immaculate arrives and the seed of  infinity houses the brothers ancestors  of the order who use  tar a substance said to be part of the  gods and their rituals they also end up  consuming the targ which caused them to  see visions of their god and making them  feel a stronger bond between the two  once collecting all of them the old  prisoner uses them to try to ascend  himself but finds out that the visions  he have been seeing aren't  of his ascension but you the players  with this knowledge in hand he is angry  and attempts to kill you once the player  defeats him they themselves can ascend  but as we have discovered  immortality isn't all that nice if  anything it's just a curse  that is mortal shell  now we get to the outro of sorts a time  where i don't have to ramble about  lore ideologies in theory a more  carefree section of the video let me  know how you enjoyed the mortal shell  story  it's definitely a complicated one filled  with subtext red herrings that were hard  to dig through but  in the end i think i came up with a  decent explanation on the game for those  who are wondering if you choose not to  ascend you actually get sent back to the  tower  like nothing ever happened if you do go  back into the hole the unchained  is alive again as we technically didn't  kill him by grabbing his gland so he is  still alive a very truly unexpected and  terrifying experience  stay tuned in the future as i plan to  cover the stories of the shells within  the game next as they are just as rich  in story as the game itself  and need to be shared thank you for  joining me on this journey if you like  the commentary like the video subscribe  for future videos coming soon  and goodbye  [Music]  you
 

